  "term": "cross-validation",
  "definition": "Cross-validation is a way of checking whether a measurement model or set of findings holds up beyond the data used to build it. In this packet, it refers to a calibration–holdout approach used during test validation to examine whether the revised model remains acceptable in a separate portion of the sample.",
